final_draft:
Thanks for the detailed report. The cause you found (numeric partition and retention intervals sent unquoted, while pgmq.create_partitioned takes text parameters) looks right, so I'll pass it to the team as a Studio bug. In the meantime, you can create the partitioned queue from the SQL editor by quoting the arguments:

select pgmq.create_partitioned('my_queue', '10000', '100000');

Queue setup is described here: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/queues/quickstart#create-queues
If you can, please share your pgmq version from: select extversion from pg_extension where extname = 'pgmq';
